WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.027
Determining the right products to sell on Amazon is a critical foundation for brand success.

00:00:07.027 --> 00:00:14.522
If you have a registered brand, Product Opportunity Explorer can help you make data-informed decisions

00:00:14.522 --> 00:00:16.395
about what to offer.

00:00:16.395 --> 00:00:23.422
This tool analyzes what products customers search for, view and purchase, helping you identify what

00:00:23.422 --> 00:00:27.638
they want and where there may be unmet demand.

00:00:27.638 --> 00:00:29.980
To access Product Opportunity Explorer,

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:36.940
open the main menu in Seller Central, hover over growth and select Product Opportunity Explorer.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:43.372
Throughout Product Opportunity Explorer, you'll see groups organized by related customer search

00:00:43.372 --> 00:00:44.980
terms called niches.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:51.812
Amazon creates these niches by analyzing which products customers tend to click on or buy after

00:00:51.812 --> 00:00:53.520
searching for specific keywords.

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:59.388
For example, customers searching for terms like stainless steel water bottle and insulated water

00:00:59.388 --> 00:01:03.580
bottle might be grouped into a single water bottle niche.

00:01:03.580 --> 00:01:11.123
Niches metrics refresh weekly and new niches are added monthly so you can stay up-to-date on emerging

00:01:11.123 --> 00:01:11.520
trends.

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:17.280
Note that search terms and products can appear in multiple niches, whether you're looking for new

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:20.520
product ideas or want to refine an existing product.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:24.868
Exploring the home page is a good place to start.

00:01:24.868 --> 00:01:30.520
You'll find real-time insights like niches for your top ASINs, recommended niches,

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:36.520
rising or declining search terms and niches where product quality could be improved.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:43.306
If you want to look for a specific product related feature or category, you can use the search bar

00:01:43.306 --> 00:01:46.520
at the top to enter a keyword or ASIN

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:53.520
or browse by category using the Find Opportunities by Categories menu in the top left corner.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:02:00.720
If you search for a keyword or select by category, you'll start in niche view which shows related

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:05.520
customer search terms, top-clicked products and demand trends for that niche.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:13.520
If you search by ASIN, you'll start in ASIN view which shows detailed product metrics for that product.

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:21.099
You can switch between niche view and ASIN view to explore both the broader niche and specific product

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:21.520
details.

00:02:21.520 --> 00:02:27.405
Note that if your search returns the error message no matching niches, it might not offer enough

00:02:27.405 --> 00:02:30.520
search volume to be included in our data set.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:33.998
Click any niche name to open the niche details page.

00:02:33.998 --> 00:02:38.520
At the top you'll see a high-level overview of that niche's performance.

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:43.520
Below that, multiple tabs break down data into key sections.

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:49.415
The Products tab displays a list of top-performing products that customers clicked on and purchased

00:02:49.415 --> 00:02:50.520
within a niche.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:57.720
Clicking on a product opens its product metrics page where you can see its sales trends and customer

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.520
review insights.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:05.520
Click into a niche within the niches product appears in section to review more in-depth insights.

00:03:05.520 --> 00:03:12.187
The Insights and Trends tab gives you access to up to two years of data to help you understand customer

00:03:12.187 --> 00:03:12.520
demand,

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:17.520
analyze your competition and track your customer service performance.

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:24.560
The customizable graph lets you compare two metrics side-by-side, helping you analyze seasonal shopping

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:28.520
patterns and spot opportunities to adjust your growth strategy.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:35.678
The Search Terms tab shows what customers search for on Amazon and which terms perform best within

00:03:35.678 --> 00:03:36.520
a niche.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:43.402
The Customer Review Insights tab summarizes positive and negative customer feedback from product

00:03:43.402 --> 00:03:45.520
reviews in a niche.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:51.836
The Returns tab uses customer-return feedback to highlight the most common reasons products within

00:03:51.836 --> 00:03:53.520
a niche are returned.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:04:00.720
Each reason is shown as a percentage of total returns to help you gauge how frequently it occurs

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:05.520
and a line graph illustrates trends for these return reasons over time.

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:12.932
Click the question mark next to any metric column header or open the metrics glossary in the top

00:04:12.932 --> 00:04:19.108
right corner of the page to see comprehensive definitions for all metrics within product opportunity

00:04:19.108 --> 00:04:19.520
explorer.

00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:26.631
To view opportunities in a different marketplace, use the Find Opportunities in drop-down just below

00:04:26.631 --> 00:04:27.520
the glossary.

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:35.020
To learn more about interpreting and actioning the data in product opportunity explorer, watch the

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:39.520
Product Opportunity Explorer Best Practices video in Seller Central.
